  "term": "transcortical motor aphasia",
  "definition": "Transcortical motor aphasia is a historically described speech disorder in which a person can hear and understand spoken words and can also recognize and understand written words, but cannot speak voluntarily, write voluntarily, or copy. In this description, repetition, reading aloud, and writing from dictation remain possible.",
